# A queue parser scoped to one heading hid the HIGH items filed above it — the conductor never saw its own gate blockers

## Symptom

Seven consecutive `automation/overnight/queue.md` STATUS entries (08-31..09-01) read "Fell
through to STAGE-1 priority #3" instead of picking up the two HIGH-priority go-live-gate
blockers filed on 08-29. `FABLE-FULL-AUDIT-2026-09-01.md` line 113: "Conductor never picked
the gate blockers."

## Root cause

Two compounding bugs, both in `setup/scripts/task_scorer.py` (`_active_lines`) and its
sibling parsers (`queue_consolidate.py`, `daily_brief.py`): (1) **parser scope** — the active-
backlog scan only starts reading from the literal string `## Active backlog` onward
(`queue_consolidate.py:80` `ACTIVE_BACKLOG_HEADING = "## Active backlog"`), so any item filed
above that heading in the file is structurally invisible to every consumer that shares the
convention; (2) **priority order** — even when visible, an unbounded self-audit backlog tier
outranked queue HIGH items in the picker's tier order, so a HIGH item competing with a large
self-audit queue would still lose.

## Fix

Commit `04f80c3f` (2026-09-01), task W3: `task_scorer._active_lines` now scans the WHOLE
queue file, not just the region after `## Active backlog`; `conductor.md` gained a new tier
2b `GATE-BLOCKING` ranked above the self-audit tier; the freeze scope was stated explicitly
("freeze = the hook's file list, nothing else") to stop conflation between "frozen" and
"invisible to the picker."

## Generalizable pattern

Any parser that scopes itself to "everything after heading X" needs an explicit test that
plants a fixture item ABOVE that heading and asserts it is still picked up (or explicitly and
intentionally excluded, documented as such) — silent scope truncation reads identically to
"there is nothing to do" and produces a queue that looks empty while carrying real HIGH
items. Sibling to L302 (a producer's own log looked healthy line by line; only the CADENCE
was wrong and nothing watched cadence) — here the SCOPE was wrong and nothing watched scope.
